 "title": "Sulfur Metabolism in Yeast and Fungi",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the sulfur metabolism in yeast and fungi, particularly in Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Candida albicans. Key entities involved include genes and proteins such as Met32, Met17, and HSU1, which play crucial roles in sulfur assimilation and utilization. The cluster also highlights the importance of sulfur-containing compounds like methionine, cysteine, and homocysteine in fermentation processes. Additionally, the relationships between these entities and other chemicals like glutathione, hydrogen sulfide, and ROS demonstrate the complex interactions within sulfur metabolism.",
